Block sanity: the test that checks every other block on its page reads which blocks the page drew once, instead of asking the page block by block, and its budget grows with the page. On a page of 291 blocks that per-block ask was 291 round trips before any checking, which put the test at ~20s against a 20s block budget: it failed 10 times out of 10 locally and intermittently in CI. The same blocks are still checked (measured: 291 swept, 0 skipped). @djay
